# Prisma Rules

## Responsibilities

- Define schema design standards and migration workflow
- Enforce repository pattern — Prisma Client never used directly in UI/actions
- Manage relations, indexes, soft deletes, and audit fields

## Best Practices

- **Single schema file**: `src/prisma/schema.prisma`
- **cuid()** for all primary keys
- **Timestamps** on every model: `createdAt`, `updatedAt`
- **Soft delete** where legally required: `deletedAt DateTime?`
- **Indexes** on foreign keys and frequently filtered columns
- **Enums** for status fields (CaseStatus, InvoiceStatus, etc.)
- **Json** fields for flexible metadata only — prefer typed columns
- Migrations: one logical change per migration, descriptive names
- Seed script for dev roles, permissions, sample data

## Coding Standards

```prisma
model Case {
  id             String     @id @default(cuid())
  organizationId String
  title          String
  status         CaseStatus @default(OPEN)
  createdAt      DateTime   @default(now())
  updatedAt      DateTime   @updatedAt
  deletedAt      DateTime?

  organization Organization @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id])
  client       Client       @relation(fields: [clientId], references: [id])

  @@index([organizationId, status])
  @@index([clientId])
  @@map("cases")
}
```

- Use `@@map` for snake_case table names in PostgreSQL
- Use `@map` for snake_case column names when needed
- Cascade rules explicit: `onDelete: Restrict` for financial records
- `$transaction` for multi-table writes

## Folder Structure

```
src/prisma/
├── schema.prisma
├── migrations/
└── seed.ts
src/lib/prisma.ts          # Singleton PrismaClient
src/repositories/          # All DB access
```

## Naming Convention

| Element | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Model | PascalCase singular | `Case`, `InvoiceLineItem` |
| Field | camelCase | `caseNumber`, `dueDate` |
| Enum | PascalCase | `CaseStatus` |
| Enum value | SCREAMING_SNAKE | `IN_PROGRESS` |
| Relation field | camelCase singular/plural | `client`, `hearings` |
| Migration | timestamp_descriptive | `20260101_add_case_tags` |

## Performance Rules

- `select` only needed fields in list queries
- Use `include` sparingly — prefer explicit joins via repository methods
- Cursor-based pagination for large tables
- Connection pooling via PgBouncer in production

## Security Rules

- Row-level filtering by `organizationId` in every repository query
- Never expose password hashes in select statements
- Audit sensitive field changes via AuditLog model

## Examples

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — Singleton client
// lib/prisma.ts
const globalForPrisma = globalThis as unknown as { prisma: PrismaClient };
export const prisma = globalForPrisma.prisma ?? new PrismaClient();
if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production') globalForPrisma.prisma = prisma;

// ✅ GOOD — Transaction
await prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => {
  const invoice = await tx.invoice.create({ data: invoiceData });
  await tx.invoiceLineItem.createMany({ data: lineItems.map(li => ({ ...li, invoiceId: invoice.id })) });
});
```

## Things to Avoid

- `prisma db push` in production — use migrations
- N+1 queries from uncontrolled `include` nesting
- Missing indexes on filter/sort columns
- Storing files in DB — store URLs/metadata only
- Raw SQL unless performance-critical and documented

## Checklist Before Finishing Any Task

- [ ] Model has createdAt/updatedAt
- [ ] Foreign keys indexed
- [ ] organizationId scoping on tenant data
- [ ] Migration created and named descriptively
- [ ] Access only through repository layer
- [ ] Cascade delete rules reviewed for data integrity
